    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "p3HiqG",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1160,
      "name": "Design notes",
      "width": 1440,
      "height": 300,
      "content": "MODEL FLAGS: one page, three tabs, cut by who is waiting and what \"yes\" does.\n\nAppeals: an owner is waiting. Ruling per label: 1 = reject (flag stays), 2 = approve (lift). Split rulings when both labels are flagged. Rows show source chip and \"also in Flagged\" when the model also sits in the review window.\nFlagged: automation flagged it, nobody disputed. Sources: hash sweep, text scan, re-detection after a lift (today's Held Detections). 1 = confirm, 2 = revert. Days left in the 30-day review window. \"also in Appeals\" chip when an appeal is open; ruling here closes the appeal with the same reason.\nFile matches: nothing is flagged yet. Unflagged model shares a file with a minor-flagged model from a different uploader. 1 = flag as minor, 2 = dismiss. Same side-by-side evidence as the hash rows.\n\nDetail pane is one component with evidence blocks that show or hide by source: Why it was flagged (always), Scanned text with highlights (text scan and re-detected), Shared file side by side (hash and file matches), What the owner says (appeals), Prior rulings (always), Model and Uploader facts (always).\n\nStays separate: Reports > Models (any violation, different actions; linked via the Reports chip), Text scan > Model rules (config), main-app Models Needing Review (publish worthiness, later port).\nOld URLs redirect: /models/flag-appeals, /models/held-detections, /models/minor-hash-matches and the main-app /moderator/minor-hash-matches."
    },
